PART 1 — Detailed Information Architecture
# VyaparNet Information Architecture v1
## Platform Structure, Navigation & User Journey Foundation

**Status:** Architecture Planning — Post-PRDv2 Freeze  
**Date:** 2026-05-22  
**Scope:** MVP Information Architecture for Buyer, Supplier, Operator, Admin  
**Segments:** Textile + Spare Parts  
**Geography:** Patna + Bihar  

---

# 1. INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE PHILOSOPHY

## 1.1 Core Principle

Information Architecture (IA) is the invisible skeleton of VyaparNet. It defines:

- Where users land
- How they navigate
- How information is structured
- How workflows flow
- How screens connect
- How roles are isolated

## 1.2 Bharat-First IA Principles

| Principle | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Low cognitive load | One screen, one primary action |
| Mobile-first | Thumb-friendly, vertical scroll |
| Visual hierarchy | Most important action highest |
| Progressive disclosure | Simple first, details on demand |
| WhatsApp fallback | Every screen has WhatsApp help |
| Segment isolation | User never sees wrong category |
| Multilingual-ready | Hindi-English labels, RTL support later |
| Low-data | Compressed images, lazy loading |
| Trust signals | Verified badges, support visible |

## 1.3 IA vs UI

IA answers:
- What goes on this screen?
- What comes next?
- How do users get there?
- What information is needed?

UI answers later:
- How does it look?
- What colors?
- What animations?
- What typography?

**IA comes before UI. Always.**

