PART 2 — Operational Governance & Freeze Architecture
# VyaparNet Information Architecture — FINAL FREEZE

## Complete, turbine &nbsp;nonvolatile, &nbsp;production-ready stack.    
**Status:** ARCHITECTURE FROZEN  
**Date:** 2025-07-18  
**Segments:** Textile + Spare Parts  
**Geography:** Patna + Bihar  

---

# SECTION 1 — INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE PHILOSOPHY

## 1.1 Core Principle

The Information Architecture (IA) is the invisible skeleton of VyaparNet. It defines:

- Where users land  
- How they navigate  
- How information is structured  
- How roles are isolated  
- How data trickles between participants  
- How power balances across the platform

## 1.2 Bharat-First IA Principles

| Principle | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Single-focus screen | Only one primary action at a time |
| Thumb-friendly layout | Big tap targets, serial scrolls |
| Viewed where priority lives | Top items first |
| Progressive revelation | Surface details only when asked |
| Always have a path home | WhatsApp or direct line back |
| Segment isolation enforced | Cross-segment defaults denied |
| Bilingual by birth | Hindi labels, English where standard, Hinglish for dabble |
| Zip-bang efficient | Lazy images, compressed first byte |

## 1.3 IA vs UI

- **IA asks:**
  - What goes on this screen?  
  - How does a user arrive here?  
  - What information is returned?  
  - What is retained, and why?

- **UI (future) answers:**  
  - How does it look?  
  - What colors?  
  - What animations?  
  - What typography?

**IA is fixed before any visual production.**  

---

# SECTION 2 — GLOBAL NAVIGATION (ALL-RULE CONSTRAINTS)

## 2.1 Per-Role Global Navigation

| Role | Global Navigation Links |
|---|---|
| **Buyer** | [Home] [Search] [Orders] [Saved Lists] [Support] |
| **Supplier** | [Orders] [Stock] [Payments] [Communicate] [Profile] |
| **Operator** | [Tasks] [QC] [Dispatch] [Comm Center] [Profile] |
| **Admin** | [Overview] [Orders] [Buyers] [Suppliers] [Catalog] [Finance] [Audit] [Setup] |

## 2.2 Cross-Segment Boundary Rule (CRITICAL)

**This is a hard platform rule. No role or screen displays information from more than one segment simultaneously, except where explicitly authorized.**

- A Textile buyer **cannot see** Spare Parts categories  
- A Spare Parts buyer **cannot receive** Textile product recommendations  
- Search indexes, sort fields, filters are segment-isolated  

Whenever a user operates across segments, a **context switch screen** explicitly restarts the viewport and flushes browser state.

---

# SECTION 3 — BUYER PWA IA

## 3.1 Platform Level: Saved Lists & Collections

Buyers have a saved-list capability. This is an IA-level feature (data + navigation), so it is defined here and not left to UI incompletion.

| List Type | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Personal list | Short-term saved products | Seasonal Sarees |
| Procurement basket | Closer to an order, false float | Summer Stock 2025 |
| Reorder shortcut | Automatic, based on prior cart success | Activa Consumables 2x |
| Seasonal list | Event-driven, prompted by system | Diwali Dress Materials |

## 3.2 Screen Hierarchy — 12 Screens Strict Limit (MVP)

```
BUYER PWA
│
├── AUTH-AREA
│   ├── 1. Login (OTP)
│   └── 2. First-Time Onboarding (Segment-Select → Business-Create → Address → GST Optional)
│
├── DASHBOARD-FRONT
│   ├── 3. Home Screen (Tabs: Home, Search, Orders, Saved, Support)
│   │       ├── Prominent Search Bar
│   │       ├── Quick-Reorder Tile
│   │       ├── Category Grid
│   │       ├── Recent Views
│   │       └── Deal/Badges
│   ├── 4. Segment-Specific Categories (Drill List)
│   │       └── Dynamic Filters + Sort
│   ├── 5. Search / Results (No-Results Exit included)
│   │       ├── Active Suggestions
│   │       └── Recent / Trending
│   └── 6. Product Detail (Image, Name, Code, Price/MOQ, Stock State, Delivery Estimate, Return Policy)
│
├── COMMERCE-FLOWS
│   ├── 7. Cart / Order Compose (Draft Flagged)
│   ├── 8. Orders List (Active | Past | Quotes)
│   └── 9. Order Tracking (Timeline + Recovery + Support Trigger)
│
└── PROFILE & SAVED
    ├── 10. Saved Lists (Collections on Bever Display; Edit, Delete, Rename)
    ├── 11. Profile & Invoices
    └── 12. Support / WhatsApp / Help
```

## 3.3 Purposeful Empty States

When content missing, provide direction and next-step context. If all content fits, example below.

| Empty State | Helper Navigation |
|---|---|
| No Orders Yet | Navigate to "Popular Products" |
| No Saved Products | Suggest "Browse Sarees / Brake Shoes" |
| No Search Results | Trigger Request Sourcing routine |
| No History | Show "Reorder" quick-starts |

## 3.4 Loading States & Connectivity

- **Skeleton loaders** are the default pattern (never blank dashed screens).  
- **CB and retry history** on every creation fail.  
- **Session restoration** if a device was severed: next launch restores the last active screen, rehydrates any unsent forms from `draft_state`.

---

# SECTION 4 — SUPPLIER PORTAL IA

## 4.1 Scope

Suppliers are critical partners but their tasks are scoped to confirmation, dispatch, and payment visibility. They never see buyer capabilities or buyer details.

## 4.2 Screen Hierarchy — 7 Screens Max

```
SUPPLIER PORTAL
│
├── DASHBOARD-FRONT
│   ├── 1. Dashboard (Score, Action List, Revenue Snapshot)
│   ├── 2. Orders (New → In Progress → Dispatched → Complete)
│   ├── 3. Stock / Price Management (Live Update by Change + Bulk Upload)
│   └── 4. Dispatch Upload (Invoice + Proof + Tracking Info)
│
├── MONEY & PROFILE
│   ├── 5. Payments (Pending / History / Settlement)
│   ├── 6. Scorecard (Metric Breakdown + Plain-English Narrative)
│   └── 7. Profile & Documents
```

## 4.3 Supplier Score Explanation (CRITICAL FOR TRUST)

Suppliers must understand why their score goes up or down. This is not hidden logic.

| Change | Points | Explanation Display |
|---|---|---|
| Excellent fulfillment rate > 95% | +3 | "Aapke deliveries aasaan hain" |
| Correct dispatch on time | +2 | "Delivery correct & fast" |
| Late dispatch by > 24 h | −2 | "Shipment mein der hui" |
| QC failure | −5 | "Product standard nahi match hua" |
| Buyer complaint confirmed | −5 | "Buyer ko issue aaya" |

`score_detail` is a **live historical log**, not just a top-line number.

---

# SECTION 5 — CITY OPERATOR DASHBOARD IA

## 5.1 Purpose

Operators work in a walking, signal-flaky world. Every screen is MOBILE-FIRST and designed for speed, visibility, and offline resilience.

## 5.2 Screen Hierarchy — 6 Screens Max

```
CITY OPERATOR DASHBOARD
│
├── 1. Today (Tasks by Urgency: Critical | High | Normal | Low)
├── 2. Stock Confirmation (List → Supplier Details → Confirm/Reject)
├── 3. QC Upload (Order Ref → Media → Status → Submit)
├── 4. Dispatch Proof (Packing, Invoice, Docket, Carrier, GPS)
├── 5. Visit Log (Supplier, Location, Photo, Notes)
└── 6. Profile & Offline Status
```

## 5.3 Offline-First Design (CRITICAL)

**All operator actions must be storable locally if network drops.**

| Action When Offline | Behavior |
|---|---|
| QC Photo Modern | Save to local device queue |
| Stock Confirm/Edit | Local conflict resolution if server state changed |
| Dispatch Proof | Save blob locally; upload when available |
| Visit Note / Lancement | Stalled in queue with explicit meta |

**Conflict detection: If local state differs from server after reconnect, operator is prompted.**

---

# SECTION 6 — ADMIN DASHBOARD IA

## 6.1 Overview

Admins see everything. But data is segmented by view and restricted by role. Nothing is noise by default.

## 6.2 Screen Hierarchy — 20 Module Max

```
ADMIN DASHBOARD
│
├── OVERVIEW
│   ├── Global Metrics (Revenue, Orders, Exceptions)
│   ├── Segment-Level Breakout
│   └── Live Operational Health Band
│
├── CORE-BUSINESS
│   ├── Orders (All States + Advanced Filter)
│   ├── Buyers (Detail, Orders, Payments, Support Threads)
│   ├── Suppliers (Onboarding, Scorecards, Catalogs, Disputes)
│   └── Catalog (Approve, Edit, Merge, Stock Sync)
│
├── OPERATIONAL-PROFICIENCY
│   ├── Procurement Board
│   ├── QC Queue
│   ├── Shipments & Tracking
│   └── Exception Center (CRITICAL)
│
├── MONEY
│   ├── Buyer Collection
│   ├── Supplier Settlement
│   ├── Disputes Settlement
│   └── Reconciliation
│
└── GOVERNANCE
    ├── Reports (Orders, Revenue, Suppliers, Geography)
    ├── Audit Log (Entity Timeline)
    └── System Config (Segments, Roles, Feature Flags)
```

## 6.3 Exception Center (CRITICAL)

One unified view for every disruptor. Powered by a priority assignment system so the admin never starts in a sea of disorder.

| Exception Type | Priority | Auto-Action |
|---|---|---|
| Order stuck > 8h | Critical | Alarm to procurement |
| Supplier score < 70 | High | Restrict new orders |
| QC fail > 2 in 7 days | High | Operator s flagged |
| Payment mismatch | Critical | Finance swo to head |
| Fraud alert | Odd Stuff | Auto-escalate |

## 6.4 Activity Timeline (Audit All Levels)

Every critical entity gets a log:

```
Order #VN-6042
11:05 AM — Order placed by buyer
11:12 AM — Availability confirmed by Operator #3
11:47 AM — Price changed +2% due to supplier request
12:03 PM — Buyer approved new rate
12:05 PM — Procurement assigned to City A
```

## 6.5 Session Recovery Across the Entire System

- **Client-side keep visible all unsaved drafts.**
- **On re-open:** return to latest user context.
- **If multiple drafts survive, show them in order as a list.**
- **Accidental close: everything is recoverable.**

---

# SECTION 7 — NOTIFICATION ARCHITECTURE (CRITICAL)

## 7.1 Notification Hub

A verified single truth of every backend event that reaches a user.

| Platform | Channel | Used For |
|---|---|---|
| In-App | Bell icon + badge | All non-urgent |
| WhatsApp | Instant Template messages | Priority high +  nudges |
| SMS | Fallback | OTP, Payment reminders |
| Email | Daily / Weekly summaries | Admin, Finance |
| Push (future) | PWA | Delivery state change |

## 7.2 Notification Types by Receiver

**For Buyers:**
- Order created, confirmed, in procurement, dispatches, delivered, issue detected
- Return state change
- Due payment reminders
- Quote speedback loop replaced by system finalized message
- Seasonal inventory stat boost sent: low stock items they should restock

**For Suppliers:**
- New request assigned for confirmation
- Deadline coming + 4 h before cut-off
- State of payment signals
- Return / dispute notices
- Scorecard movements, clear rewards

**For Operators:**
- Task assigned with correct urgency response protocol
- Offline queues synced
- Urgent hit-and-resolve situations

**For Admins:**
- Exception firehose display
- System health pulse
- Fraud alerts
- Pipeline stuck signals

---

# SECTION 8 — UNIVERSAL COMMERCE INBOX (FUTURE-READY)

One message center for all interaction.

| Thread Type | Example |
|---|---|
| Order support | "Order adjusted after QC" |
| Supplier threads | "Given price 3% more on urgent shipment" |
| Sourcing requests | "Can you get this in 6 days?" |
| Dispute threads | "Rejected due to->___ evidence attached" |

MVP: WhatsApp fallback only, inbox monitor for admin.  
Phase 2+: Quotient rename after platform-native conversation.

---

# SECTION 9 — DRAFT STATES (ALL ROLES)

Every role supports autosaved work-in-progress.

| Role | Draft Capabilities |
|---|---|
| Buyer | Draft order, draft quotation request, saved procurement lists |
| Supplier | Draft listing, draft stock update, draft dispatch |
| Operator | Draft QC, draft visit note, draft dispatch proof |
| Admin | Draft approvals, draft timeline, draft save resolution |

Save logic: local timestamp → server sync on opportunity.  
Behavior: flush on submit; otherwise flush to a dedicated `/drafts` API.

---

# SECTION 10 — DYNAMIC TAXONOMY ARCHITECTURE

No Name工匠 categories. Name engine changes.

| Current Part | Current Options | Future Expandibility |
|---|---|---|
| Segments  | Textile, Spare Parts | Pharma by entering new liquid name and metadata set |
| Vehicle tree | 2W / 4W / Truck / Heavy | Commercial / 3W inserted by a mapping subsystem  |
| Serving materials | Sarees, Fabrics, Handlooms, etc. | Future metro consumer by software activation |
| Textile fiber | Cotton, Silk, Synthetic, Mixed | Future category is textile synthetic steel |

Built via a `category_config` + `category_attributes` + `category_taxonomy` engine in the code.

---

# SECTION 11 — OPERATIONAL OWNERSHIP TRACKING

Every workflow entity MUST have a visible assignee at all time.

| Entity | Owner | Backup Owner |
|---|---|---|
| Order | Supplier | Procurement Manager |
| Procurement Task | City Operator | Ops Manager |
| QC | City Operator | Ops Manager |
| Shipment | Logistics | Supplier |
| Dispute | Admin | Senior Admin |
| Exception | Ops Manager | Admin Lead |

Owner change must leave a **reason a trail** in the activity timeline.

---

# SECTION 12 — FALLBACK HUMAN ESCALATION PHILOSOPHY

**If automation fails, a human agent accepts the work in less than 1 escalation jump.**

| Scenario | Fallback Path |
|---|---|
| Automated supplier trigger fails | Human operator picks, buyer notified |
| Price round-trip day deadline | Human operator intervenes after warning |
| QC NOT performed in time | Admin receives escalated alert |
| Payment reconciliation failure | Human finance reviews directly |
| Exception center  high crossed | Founder on every >6 hrs delay |

---

# SECTION 13 — INDEPENDENT PLATFORMS (ALL TOOLS)

## 13.1 Help / Education In-System

| Mode | Content |
|---|---|
| Mini-tour | First-time buyer onboard |
| Tooltips | Hover (desktop) / tap-and-hold (mobile) |
| "Kaise order karein" | 30-second GIF examples |
| Contextual hint | "Usa query `OL` search spread" |
| WhatsApp help | Direct human path always in global bar |

## 13.2 Final Score: Operational Readiness Check

| Capability | Status |
|---|---|
| Segment cross-protection | Enforced at router + search + filter + product surface |
| Notification hub | Multi-channel, per-role, priority defined |
| Taskeings priority model | Critical / High / Normal / Low enforced |
| Saved lists present | Collections managed at buyer and operator |
| Supplier score explanation | Narrative-aware, not number-only |
| Offline operator → conflict detect | Web storage + sync + conflict UI |
| Empty states | Standardized per-screen and topic |
| Loading skeletons | Default user expectation |
| Session recovery | Auto-rehydration at open |
| Ownership traceability | All entities / all views / all roles |
| Escalation fallbacks | Human recovery is architecturally always possible |
| Dynamic taxonomy | Ready for new segments without recompile |
| Draft states | All roles, all primary flows, never lost |
| Universal inbox | Placeholder parallel to WhatsApp always |
| Help & education | Minimal, but structurally present in all role flows |
| Language accessibility | Hindi-first with fallback, not polyglot default |

